{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"- **Borrower/default risk:** The borrower fails to return securities. Controls include credit screening, exposure limits, monitoring and enforceable lending agreements.\n- **Collateral-shortfall risk:** Collateral liquidation proceeds may not cover replacement securities because of market moves, FX changes, illiquidity or enforcement costs. Controls include haircuts, daily marking-to-market, margin calls and liquid, diversified collateral.\n- **Cash-reinvestment risk:** Investments purchased with cash collateral suffer credit losses, price declines or liquidity mismatches. Controls include conservative eligibility, diversification, short maturities and liquidity buffers.\n\n**U.S. iShares example:** The lending bank/agent’s borrower-default indemnity addresses covered shortfalls under its contractual terms; it does **not** generally insure cash-reinvestment losses. U.S. collateral practices are not UCITS rules.\n\n**UCITS:** Funds must be able to recall lent securities or terminate lending arrangements at any time. ESMA collateral standards address liquidity, valuation, credit quality, diversification and custody; noncash collateral cannot be reinvested, while cash reinvestment is restricted.\n\n**Collateral reduces—not eliminates—potential losses.**"}}
